@@ -9,6 +9,31 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start

 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.

+## Agent tools
+
+Hydrated React components expose the following client-side tools through
+[WebMCP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/webmcp/agentic-javascript-tools)
+using Chrome's `use-webmcp-tool` integration:
+
+| Tool | Available on | Arguments | Action |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `sign_in` | Sign-in page | `username`, `password` | Submit the login form and display its result. |
+| `sign_up` | Sign-up page | `username`, `password` | Register an account and display its result. Passwords require eight characters and a number. |
+| `search_articles` | Pages with the main header | `query` | Open search, display matching titles/summaries, and return articles with links. |
+
+Tools share the UI's handlers and validation. Authentication results include success/error
+messages, never passwords or tokens. Requests support cancellation and reject overlapping
+submissions. Tools unregister when their components unmount, including page navigation.
+
+Agent discovery requires a browser exposing the experimental `document.modelContext`
+API in a secure context. Browsers without WebMCP retain the normal UI. No backend MCP
+server or polyfill is required. Authentication still uses the existing remote login and
+registration service.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated tool tests with mocked browser registration and HTTP
+responses, and `pnpm run build` to build the application. Tests do not start a server
+or contact the authentication service.
+
