+# smallpt — browser edition
+
+Kevin Beason's [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) C++ path tracer, compiled to WebAssembly with Emscripten. All tracing happens in a dedicated module Web Worker on the visitor's CPU. No server-side rendering, pthreads, or cross-origin isolation headers are required.
+
+Open the site using an HTTP(S) static host (module workers cannot run from `file://`). `index.html` starts a 640 × 480, 64-sample render automatically. Randomize colors rerenders the walls, mirror sphere, and glass sphere with new reflectance colors. Reset restores the original palette. The quality slider selects 16, 64, 128, or 256 samples per pixel. Save image downloads the current render as PNG.
+
+## Build
+
+Requires Emscripten (`em++`, tested with 6.0.5) on PATH. No npm dependencies are required.
+
+```sh
+npm run build
+```
+
+This compiles `src/renderer.cpp` to `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm`, then packages the complete static site in `dist/`. Compiled assets are also included at the repository root so the existing static host can serve it directly. Serve `.wasm` as `application/wasm` for streaming compilation; Emscripten also supports a byte-buffer fallback.
+
+The original smallpt radiance function, sphere geometry, materials, camera and sampling pattern are retained. The adapter replaces the CLI/PPM output with progressive four-sample passes, accumulates linear radiance before gamma encoding, and exposes one RGBA buffer. Rows are batched in C++ and frame buffers transferred from the worker. New renders cancel previous work between row strips. A 256-sample native render of the same adapter is included as the initial preview.
+
+Upstream `vendor/smallpt/smallpt.cpp` has only a `SMALLPT_LIBRARY` guard around its original CLI main. Original copyright and MIT license are preserved in `vendor/smallpt/LICENSE.txt`.
+
+`npm run check:wasm` executes the compiled artifact directly in Node and checks opaque RGBA pixels, deterministic reset, palette changes, and progressive accumulation.
+
