+# smallpt / a study in light
+
+Kevin Beason's MIT-licensed C++ path tracer compiled to actual WebAssembly with Emscripten. Open `index.html` through a static host. No backend, runtime dependencies, cross-origin isolation, or GPU is required.
+
+The page renders automatically in a dedicated Web Worker. Each pass adds four tent-filtered camera samples per pixel; frames are displayed after each pass. Randomize changes the wall and sphere reflectances and restarts the tracer with a fresh cryptographic seed. Controls support pause/resume, sample count, resolution, original-palette reset, fullscreen, and saving the current canvas as PNG.
+
+- `npm run build` recompiles the C++ and creates the deployable static `dist/` folder. Requires `em++` (Emscripten).
+- `npm test` checks actual WASM pixel output, repeatable seeds, and randomized sphere reflectances in Node.
+- Generated `assets/smallpt.js` and `assets/smallpt.wasm` are committed so static hosting needs no compiler.
+- `assets/preview.png` is an initial 128-spp render produced by the same WASM binary. Live output replaces it after the first completed pass.
+
+`vendor/smallpt.cpp` is the unmodified upstream source: https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.txt. The original MIT license is in `vendor/LICENSE.txt`. `src/smallpt.cpp` preserves the original ray intersection and radiance code and replaces the CLI image writer with an incremental C API. The browser adapter averages unclamped linear radiance before display gamma, rather than clamping each subpixel. The upstream 99-line implementation uses OpenMP; this port uses a single dedicated worker and yields between row batches.
