@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+# smallpt in the browser
+
+The unchanged `smallpt-original.cpp` is Kevin Beason's MIT-licensed source:
+https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/smallpt.txt
+
+`smallpt-wasm.cpp` wraps the original radiance integrator with exported initialization and row-rendering functions. It replaces PPM file output with an RGBA memory buffer, accumulates four samples per pixel per pass, and exposes reflectance colors. The two sphere materials remain mirror and glass, with randomized tints; the corresponding walls use the same palette. Rendering runs in a module Web Worker, independent of the UI thread. A new request terminates the previous worker.
+
+The initial reference PNG is the original render from the smallpt distribution. Once the first browser-computed pass is ready, the canvas replaces it.
+
+## Build
+
+With Emscripten's `em++` on PATH:
+
+    pnpm build:wasm
+    pnpm check:wasm
+    pnpm build
+
+The compiled JS and WASM are checked in under `public/wasm`, so the normal app build does not require Emscripten. Astro prerenders the home page to `dist/client/index.html`; that file and its static assets can be hosted independently. Use HTTP(S) hosting, since module workers are not supported over file URLs. No cross-origin isolation or shared memory is required.
+
+The smoke check executes the actual WASM binary in Node without starting a server or importing the application server. It checks RGBA output, changes from new colors, and accumulator resets.
+
+The MIT license is preserved in `LICENSE.txt` and linked from the page.
