+# The Daily Grind
+
+The static page loads `coffee-card.js` as a browser module. No build is required.
+Each autonomous `<coffee-card>` preserves its light DOM fallback content and
+enhances it when registered. Existing heading, description, and link nodes are
+reused so updates preserve focus. Cards created with `document.createElement`
+receive the same markup when connected.
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | string | Coffee heading; defaults to an empty string. |
+| `description` | string | Description; defaults to an empty string. |
+| `href` | string | Details destination; relative and HTTP(S) URLs are supported. |
+| `price` | number | Optional USD price; hidden when the attribute is absent. Invalid, negative, or non-finite values read as zero. |
+| `disabled` | boolean | Presence disables the details link, updates its accessible state, and removes it from the tab order. |
+
+String property assignments serialize to attributes; `null` or `undefined`
+removes them. Numeric assignments serialize to a finite nonnegative value;
+`null` or `undefined` removes the price. Boolean properties use truthiness and
+reflect by adding/removing the attribute. As with native boolean attributes,
+`disabled="false"` still means disabled; use `card.disabled = false` or remove
+the attribute to enable the card.
+
+```js
+const card = document.querySelector('coffee-card');
+card.name = 'Maple Oat Latte';
+card.price = 5.5; // price="5.5", displayed as $5.50
+card.disabled = true;
+card.removeAttribute('disabled'); // property reads false; link is enabled
+```
+
+Attribute changes update the card immediately. Properties assigned before
+registration are replayed through the reflected setters on connection. Connection
+and disconnection attach and remove the link's click guard, and reconnecting
+preserves the card's nodes and state.
