+# The Daily Grind
+
+Coffee cards are autonomous `<coffee-card>` custom elements. Import `coffee-card.js`
+once with a module script; each card owns its markup and styles in an open shadow
+root and inherits the page's font, colors, and CSS theme variables.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card
+  name="Maple Oat Latte"
+  description="Creamy oat milk with Vermont maple syrup."
+  href="/menu/seasonal"
+  price="5.50"
+  featured
+></coffee-card>
+```
+
+Attributes and properties stay in sync, and updates immediately render:
+
+| Attribute / property | Type | Default / behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `name` | String | Empty string |
+| `description` | String | Empty string |
+| `href` | String | `/menu`; links accept relative paths and HTTP(S) URLs |
+| `price` | Number | `0`; hidden when the attribute is absent; formatted as USD |
+| `featured` | Boolean | `false`; presence shows a Featured label |
+
+Setting a string property to `null` or `undefined` removes its attribute.
+Prices accept finite, nonnegative numbers; invalid values read/render as `0`.
+Setting `price` to `null` or `undefined` removes the price. Boolean attributes use
+HTML presence semantics: `featured="false"` is still true; assign
+`card.featured = false` or remove the attribute to turn it off.
+
+On connection, the element renders, upgrades any properties assigned before
+registration, and attaches its link listener. On disconnection, it removes that
+listener; reconnection restores it. Clicking View Details emits a bubbling,
+composed, cancelable `coffee-select` event with `{ name, href, price, featured }`
+in `event.detail`. Calling `preventDefault()` on that event cancels navigation.
+
+Run `pnpm install` and `pnpm test` for DOM-based reflection and lifecycle tests.
+No build step is required.
