+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static, responsive coffee workspace with local receipt and gift voucher signing.
+No build step or runtime dependencies are needed. Serve the files over HTTPS
+(or localhost) so Web Crypto is available. Browser IndexedDB storage is required.
+
+## Digital signatures
+
+- Classical ECDSA P-256 with SHA-256, using the browser's Web Crypto API.
+- The private CryptoKey is non-exportable and persisted in IndexedDB. The public
+  key is exportable as JWK; its identifier is the SHA-256 digest of its SPKI bytes.
+- A versioned JSON envelope signs `version`, `algorithm`, `keyId`, and `payload`.
+  JSON object keys are recursively sorted before UTF-8 encoding. Arrays preserve
+  their order. The signature is standard Base64 of the 64-byte ECDSA P1363 result.
+- Verification uses only this workspace's saved public key, never a key supplied
+  by a document. Unsupported schemas, unknown keys, or invalid signatures fail.
+- Locally stored documents are verified again before displaying history. The
+  most recent five are shown; counters include all valid saved documents.
+
+This is a local signing workspace, not a merchant issuing authority. A valid
+signature establishes that the saved browser key signed the unchanged contents;
+it does not prove payment, a real merchant's identity, or voucher redemption
+eligibility. Public keys must be exchanged through a trusted channel for
+independent verification. Clearing browser site data removes the signing key
+and local history. Exporting a public key cannot back up the private key.
+
+`npm test` runs cryptographic checks in Node.js 22+, without a browser or server.
