+Client-side paint monitoring
+===========================
+
+`performance-monitor.js` loads with `defer` and preserves existing links. Navigation,
+Order Now, and Seasonal Favorites are identified by `data-performance-target`.
+It observes `interaction-contentful-paint` and `soft-navigation` only when the
+browser advertises support. Unsupported browsers skip those metrics; there is no
+synthetic timer fallback that claims to measure asynchronous content rendering.
+
+Read the last 100 reports with `window.dailyGrindPerformance.reports`, or attach
+an analytics adapter with:
+
+```js
+window.addEventListener('daily-grind:performance', ({ detail }) => {
+  // Send detail to your existing analytics collector.
+});
+```
+
+No network collector or third-party dependency is added. Reports contain static
+target names and destination pathnames, without query strings or DOM references.
+Support flags are available under `window.dailyGrindPerformance.supported`.
+
+`interaction-paint` reports include `interactionId`, `target`, `destination`,
+`startTime`, `duration` (milliseconds from interaction start to presentation), and
+the largest painted content's `size`. Each larger contentful paint produces a new
+candidate report for the same interaction; consumers should update by interaction
+ID rather than counting candidates as separate clicks. Event Timing IDs and
+captured trusted input timestamps associate the source with its asynchronous paints.
+
+`soft-navigation` reports include the route's `interactionId`, `navigationId`,
+`destination`, `startTime`, `fcpDuration`, `lcpDuration`, and `size`. They finalize
+when another soft navigation occurs or the page is hidden/departed. LCP starts
+with `getLargestInteractionContentfulPaint()` and subsequent paints match by
+interaction ID, including paints carrying the previous navigation ID.
+
+These are contentful-paint metrics, not a guarantee that all animations or all
+future asynchronous work have completed. No-paint clicks produce no paint report.
+The current site uses full-document links: destination document rendering cannot
+be measured by the departing homepage's observers. Client-side view switches are
+measured automatically when the browser detects a soft navigation (a trusted
+interaction causing contentful rendering and a URL change). No router is added.
+
+Run automated checks without a server or browser:
+
+```sh
+node --check performance-monitor.js
+node --test performance-monitor.test.cjs
+```
