@@ -15,3 +15,42 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Account settings and passkeys
+
+Readers can manage passkeys at `/devtools-times/account/settings` after signing in.
+Sign-in stores the identity service token in the server-side Astro session, never in browser storage.
+Configure shared durable Astro session storage for deployments with multiple server instances.
+
+The external identity service owns the credential database and must implement the following contract.
+Set server-only `IDENTITY_API_URL` to override the existing `times_cdn/api` service base URL.
+These endpoints are an integration requirement; their implementation is outside this repository.
+
+- `POST /login`: accepts `{ username, password }`, returns `{ token }`.
+- `GET /credentials`: authenticates the bearer token and returns the **complete** account list as `{ rpId, userId, credentials }`.
+  Each credential contains `{ id, name, aaguid?, registeredAt, lastUsedAt? }`; timestamps are epoch milliseconds.
+- `PUT /credential/:id`: authenticates the bearer token, verifies account ownership, and persists `{ name }` (1–80 characters).
+- `DELETE /credential/:id`: authenticates the bearer token, verifies account ownership, and deletes the credential.
+
+The service must enforce token expiry, ownership, and persistent updates. `rpId` must match the registration RP ID;
+`userId` and all credential IDs must be valid unpadded Base64URL. Never return a paginated/partial credential list:
+browser synchronization treats the list as authoritative, including an empty list after the final removal.
+Missing service support produces a visible error rather than a fabricated local passkey list.
+
+The settings page signals accepted credentials on load and after successful mutations and an authoritative refetch.
+Individual passkey display names are account labels, so renaming them does not change WebAuthn user profile details.
+Browsers without the Signal API retain full server-side management with manual password-manager cleanup guidance.
+Passkey registration and account profile editing are outside this management section.
+
+Provider labels and selected optimized icons come from the [passkey-authenticator-aaguids registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Unknown or anonymized providers use a generic key icon; AAGUIDs are only display hints.
+
+Run focused logic tests with `node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/passkeys.test.ts`.
+For API handler tests, run:
+
+```sh
+pnpm dlx esbuild tests/account-api.test.ts --bundle --platform=node --format=esm --define:import.meta.env='{}' --outfile=/tmp/devtools-account-api.test.mjs
+node --test /tmp/devtools-account-api.test.mjs
+```
+
+These tests mock the external identity service and do not start a server or import the built server entrypoint.
