 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account settings
+
+Sign in and sign up retain the existing remote username/password service. A successful
+password login establishes an HTTP-only local session and associates the exact username
+with a random WebAuthn user ID. Passwords are forwarded only to the existing account
+service and are never stored locally. After signing up or signing in, users can create a
+passkey, or continue to `/devtools-times/account/settings` to manage their account.
+The original username remains the password login identifier; the display name is editable.
+
+Passkeys use native WebAuthn browser APIs, with compatibility polyfills for JSON conversion
+and capability detection, and SimpleWebAuthn for server signature verification. Registration
+requires discoverable credentials and user verification. Reauthentication is restricted to
+the signed-in account's keys; adding keys and changing settings require verification within
+five minutes. Removal has an explicit confirmation and reauthentication step. A password
+remains available if the last passkey is removed. Browser password-manager synchronization
+is optional and feature-detected. Provider names use the community
+[passkey AAGUID registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids);
+unknown providers use a generic passkey label/icon, and provider data never controls access.
+
+Runtime requirements:
+
+- Node.js 24 or newer (uses built-in SQLite).
+- HTTPS, or localhost during local development.
+- `PASSKEY_ORIGIN`: the public origin, for example `https://news.example.com` (no path).
+  Set this explicitly in production, particularly behind a proxy. Without it, the server
+  uses the request URL origin. Auth mutations enforce a matching Origin header.
+- `PASSKEY_RP_ID`: the relying-party domain, for example `news.example.com`. Defaults to
+  the configured origin's hostname. Keep this value stable after registering passkeys.
+- `AUTH_DB_PATH`: SQLite file path; defaults to `./data/auth.sqlite`. Mount persistent,
+  writable storage. This database stores public credentials, hashed session tokens, and
+  short-lived single-use challenges. It must be shared by every process serving the app;
+  multi-host deployments should replace this store with a shared database. Ephemeral
+  instance storage will lose passkeys and sessions on replacement.
+
+The `api/auth/*` routes handle password login/signup, logout, passkey ceremonies,
+reauthentication, profile updates, and passkey management. API responses are private and
+uncached, and management routes enforce ownership on the server.
