+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static, dependency-free website. Run `npm test` for privacy regression checks and
+`npm run build` to create `dist/`. No server is needed for either command.
+
+## Deploying the security headers
+
+Publish **dist/** on Netlify or Cloudflare Pages to apply its generated `_headers`
+file to every route, including the privacy page and assets. For another host,
+configure equivalent response headers from `security-headers.json` at the origin
+or CDN. A generic static server (including the existing development `start`
+command) does not necessarily honor `_headers`. Build success does not establish
+that a deployed host serves headers.
+
+Serve production over HTTPS and redirect HTTP to HTTPS at the host. HSTS applies
+to this hostname only; subdomain coverage and preloading are deliberately not
+assumed. The meta CSP/referrer policy provide fallback protection, but framing,
+permissions, HSTS, cache, and isolation policies require HTTP response headers.
+See [MDN on frame-ancestors](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/frame-ancestors).
+
+## Data handling and third-party audit
+
+- The original Unsplash hero URL exposed visitor connection information to a
+  third party. The same stock photo is now downloaded into `assets/coffee-hero.jpg`
+  and served locally. Source:
+  https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085.
+  No visitor request to Unsplash is necessary.
+- There are no runtime scripts, application packages, analytics, embeds, external
+  fonts, tracking pixels, forms, cookies, browser storage, or service workers.
+  Keep this inventory current when changing assets or dependencies. The optional
+  development `start` command downloads `statikk` through `pnpm dlx`; it is not a
+  production deployment or part of the dependency-free build.
+- CSP denies scripts, connections, workers, frames, and form submissions. Only
+  same-origin CSS and images are allowed. Do not loosen it for a new vendor until
+  documenting purpose, minimum data, consent needs, recipients, retention,
+  deletion, security review, and a less intrusive alternative. Re-audit before
+  each release and whenever a dependency or integration changes.
+- No personal data is collected by application code. Do not introduce logging
+  of page queries, identifiers, secrets, or user content. No CSP report endpoint
+  is configured, to avoid creating a new collection channel.
+- Before public deployment, identify the hosting processor, document its access
+  and security logs and actual retention/deletion policy, minimize those logs,
+  restrict staff access, and update the privacy notice. Do not promise that a
+  CDN or hosting service keeps no logs.
+- Existing account, ordering, contact, and rewards destinations are placeholders;
+  no backend exists here. Removed the unconditional GET logout link because this
+  static site has no authenticated session. A future backend must validate inputs,
+  use TLS and authenticated authorization checks, protect state changes with POST
+  and CSRF defenses, use Secure/HttpOnly/SameSite session cookies, avoid personal
+  data in URLs or browser storage, disable sensitive response caching, encrypt
+  stored data, and enforce explicit retention and deletion periods. Do not add
+  collection forms before those controls and their privacy notice exist.
+
+The public privacy page describes this static website only. These changes are a
+source review and automated regression checks, not an independent external audit
+or a verification of hosting behavior.
