+# Daily Grind
+
+Run `npm start` with Node.js 20 or later to serve the site (default port 11222;
+override with `PORT`). No dependencies or build step are required.
+
+Newsletter submissions go to the same-origin `POST /api/newsletter` endpoint.
+Validated addresses and signup timestamps are appended to `data/newsletter.jsonl`.
+Set `DATA_DIR` to a persistent writable directory in deployments. This file is
+private to the server and excluded from Git. Connect your newsletter delivery
+process to this list; this application stores subscriptions but does not send mail.
+
+The Node server sets Content-Security-Policy on every response. Scripts and styles
+must come from this origin, connections and form submissions stay on this origin,
+and images may additionally load from `https://images.unsplash.com`. Inline scripts,
+inline styles, plugins, frames, and base URL overrides are blocked. Keep this header
+when placing the server behind a reverse proxy. CSP restricts these resource and
+connection types; it is not a substitute for preventing script injection or a
+general restriction on top-level browser navigation.
+
+Run `npm test` for automated handler and client checks. Tests use in-memory requests
+and a simulated DOM; they do not start a server or open a browser.
