+# Security audit and deployment
+
+`npm start` runs the dependency-free Node HTTP server. `PORT` defaults to `11222`.
+`npm run build` performs syntax checks without starting or importing the server.
+
+## Changes from the audit
+
+- Extracted the inline stylesheet and heading style into `styles.css`, preserving
+  the existing design. There are no inline scripts, event handlers, or styles.
+- The main page needs no JavaScript, so its policy blocks all scripts. The logout
+  page permits only its cleanup script using a fresh cryptographic nonce on every
+  response. No dynamic HTML injection, string evaluation, third-party scripts, or
+  Trusted Types policies are used. Trusted Types enforcement blocks future unsafe
+  DOM injection sinks in browsers that support it.
+- CSP denies resources by default, allows local CSS and the existing Unsplash
+  photograph, and blocks framing, plugins, base URL changes, and inline handlers.
+  The same security headers cover errors, assets, and unsupported methods.
+- Responses disable caching, MIME sniffing, referrer disclosure, framing, and
+  unused device permissions. Cross-origin opener and resource policies isolate
+  this site's documents and resources. COEP is deliberately omitted because the
+  existing external photograph does not require cross-origin isolation.
+- Public files are explicitly allowlisted. Repository files cannot be requested.
+  Existing navigation URLs still display the original page; unknown URLs return
+  404. Unsupported methods return 405. URL parsing does not trust the Host header.
+
+## Logout behavior and limits
+
+`GET /logout` (also `/logout/` and POST) returns a confirmation page with
+`Clear-Site-Data: "cache", "cookies", "storage"` and `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+It also expires received cookies at `Path=/`. A nonce-authorized external script
+clears local/session storage, Cache Storage, and service worker registrations as
+a best-effort fallback. It never inserts HTML or evaluates strings.
+
+There is no login implementation, session database, or token issuer in this
+repository. If authentication is added, revoke the visitor's session or refresh
+token on the server before returning the logout response. Cookie expiry alone
+cannot revoke a copied token. Configure explicit cookie expiry for any future
+authentication cookies with non-root paths or Domain attributes.
+
+Full browser data clearing requires HTTPS and browser support for
+[Clear-Site-Data](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Clear-Site-Data).
+Its cookie clearing can affect other subdomains of the same registered domain;
+deploy on an appropriately isolated domain. The fallback cannot reliably clear
+every storage type (such as IndexedDB) or every cookie scope. Other open tabs may
+retain in-memory state. With JavaScript disabled, server-driven clearing still
+works in supporting browsers.
+
+## Deploying policies
+
+Terminate HTTPS at the deployment edge, preserve the Node response headers, and
+set `HTTPS_ONLY=true` once HTTPS is configured. This enables HSTS and Secure on
+ordinary cookie deletion headers. The server does not trust forwarded protocol
+headers, and does not enable HSTS on local HTTP. No wildcard subdomain HSTS or
+preload commitment is made.
+
+The enforced CSP matches the audited resources; it needs no `unsafe-inline` or
+`unsafe-eval` exceptions. Before adding integrations, audit their resource and DOM
+requirements. Trial a proposed tighter policy using `Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only`
+alongside the existing enforced policy, with an appropriate reporting service if
+needed. Do not replace the enforced policy with a report-only header. See
+[CSP guidance](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP) and
+[Trusted Types enforcement](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Content-Security-Policy/require-trusted-types-for).
+
+Verification for this change is limited to syntax, static markup/resource checks,
+and diff review. No browser, listening server, or server entrypoint import was used.
