+# SMS verification integration
+
+This repository is a static homepage. `verification.js` implements the client flow and calls the following same-origin JSON endpoints. Until a backend supplies them, the page reports that text sign-in is unavailable; it never fabricates an SMS or authenticates a code locally.
+
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/send`: accept `{ "phone": "+14155550123", "purpose": "rewards" }` (or `"order"`). Return `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-generated-id" }` after dispatching the text.
+- `POST /api/auth/sms/verify`: accept `{ "challengeId": "…", "code": "012345", "purpose": "rewards" }`. Validate the challenge server-side, establish an authenticated session using a Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookie, and return `{ "verified": true }` only on success. The client navigates to `/rewards` or `/order-online`.
+
+Both destination pages must enforce session authentication. Treat purpose as a navigation preference, never as an authorization claim. Reject cross-origin requests (validate Origin / use CSRF protections); validate phone numbers and codes independently of the client. Generate codes securely, bind challenges to the browser session and number, expire them promptly, invalidate prior codes on resend, consume codes once, and rate-limit send and verify requests by session, number, and IP. Avoid revealing whether a number has an account. Never log codes. Return 400/401 for invalid codes, 410 for expired challenges, and 429 for throttling. Server limits are required; the client's 30-second cooldown is only a UI affordance.
+
+## Outgoing text format
+
+Use the actual deployed hostname (no scheme, port, or path). The domain-binding line must be the very last line:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind sign-in code is 012345.
+
+@your-deployed-hostname.com #012345
+```
+
+Serve over HTTPS. The client starts a feature-detected WebOTP request before dispatching the text, cancels it on submission, resend, phone changes, timeout, or page exit, and uses `requestSubmit()` so validation and the application handler run. On other browsers, the single `autocomplete="one-time-code"` field supports system suggestions, pasting, and manual entry. No SMS-reading polyfill is needed.
+
+Stock photography is sourced from Unsplash and stored in `assets/`. No development server is needed to edit the page.
