+use WebOTP over HTTPS, with manual entry and paste available everywhere. Configure
+the Twilio SMS template to end with the origin-bound format required by WebOTP:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 123456.
+
+@your-deployed-host.example #123456
+```
+
+Use the actual host (without scheme or path) and the dynamically inserted code in
+the template. WebOTP requests are canceled when the form changes, is submitted,
+or after two minutes. Extracted codes remain visible for the user to submit.
+See the [WebOTP documentation](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/WebOTP_API)
+and [Twilio Verify documentation](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api).
