+# The Daily Grind
+
+This static page loads `page.mjs` for ordering messages, redirect validation,
+link classification, and a sandboxed daily coffee tip widget.
+
+Deployment configuration lives in `validation.mjs`: the assumed trusted ordering
+origin is `https://orders.dailygrind.coffee`, and the explicitly controlled site
+domain is `dailygrind.coffee`. Update these to the real owned domains before
+connecting an ordering service. The current page URL is the site reference.
+
+Ordering messages must come from that exact origin, with one of these payloads:
+
+- `{ type: 'order-status', text: 'Your order is ready.' }` updates status as text.
+- `{ type: 'redirect', url: '/account' }` navigates only after same-site validation.
+
+Only HTTP(S) links without URL credentials are allowed. External links remain
+usable and receive `external noopener noreferrer` relationship tokens. Site
+checks use the native `Origin` API where supported. Without it, cross-subdomain
+navigation is allowed only within the explicitly configured owned domain;
+other deployments conservatively allow only the same scheme and hostname.
+No registrable domain is inferred by splitting hostnames.
+
+The widget must send `init` first. Its expected window and opaque origin are pinned
+once; unrelated sandboxed frames cannot initialize or send accepted updates.
+Browsers without `Origin` use exact `event.source` identity and require `"null"`.
+That fallback cannot detect navigation of the same window to a different opaque
+document; use a dedicated MessageChannel if that stronger lifecycle boundary is
+needed on those browsers. The native path rejects a changed opaque origin.
+
+Run the focused checks with `npm test`. Native opaque-origin extraction requires
+a browser; Node tests model that platform boundary and exercise the fallback
+directly. No server or build step is required for these checks.
