@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Daily Grind
+
+Node 24+ and pnpm are required. Install with `pnpm install`. Run `pnpm build`
+for syntax checks and `pnpm test` for automated verification. `pnpm start`
+serves the homepage and registration endpoint together (default port 11222).
+
+## Deployment
+
+Set `PUBLIC_ORIGIN` to the exact public HTTPS origin, and `NODE_ENV=production`.
+Set `EMAIL_VERIFICATION_ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN` to a valid token registered for that
+origin at https://developer.chrome.com/origintrials/. Environment variables
+must be supplied by the hosting platform or shell; `.env.example` documents them.
+The app does not automatically load an `.env` file.
+
+The Email Verification API is experimental, currently in Chrome's origin trial.
+See https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/email-verification for supported
+versions and providers. The customer must be signed in to a participating email
+provider in the same browser. The trial token is deployment-specific and cannot
+be supplied in source code. Unsupported browsers, signed-out users, and invalid
+tokens receive an honest retry message; **no OTP or magic link is sent**, and no
+account is created until ownership is verified.
+
+The homepage is server-rendered with a fresh 256-bit nonce, stored in SQLite and
+bound to an HttpOnly session cookie. It must be served by `server.mjs`, not a
+static file host. All form submissions work without JavaScript. The server
+consumes the nonce atomically, verifies DNS issuer delegation, issuer metadata,
+EVT signature and freshness, browser key binding signature, audience, nonce,
+and SD-JWT hash binding before storing a verified rewards account. Both issuer
+and key binding use an explicit asymmetric algorithm allowlist. Provider HTTP
+requests are time- and size-limited, reject redirects, and pin DNS resolution to
+public IP addresses to prevent server-side request forgery.
+
+Mount `data/` on persistent storage (or set `DATABASE_PATH`). SQLite stores names,
+email addresses and verification timestamps; protect this personal data with
+appropriate filesystem access and backups. SQLite nonce consumption supports
+multiple processes sharing one local database. For horizontally distributed
+deployments, move accounts and nonce consumption to a shared transactional store.
+Apply hosting-level rate limits to the homepage and POST `/api/verify-email`.
+Email verification establishes ownership, not inbox deliverability or a future
+login method; this change does not implement account login or rewards redemption.
+
+No development server, preview server, or manual browser verification was used
+to implement or validate this change.
