+</style>
+</head>
+<body>
+<header><div class="nav"><div class="brand"><span class="brand-icon" aria-hidden="true">t.</span> typeform<span style="font-size:.6rem;letter-spacing:0;color:#9ba393;margin-left:5px;font-weight:400">/ labs</span></div><span class="nav-note"><span class="status-dot"></span>A typography experiment</span></div></header>
+<main>
+<div class="eyebrow">Small details. Better type.</div>
+<h1>Different fonts. Same rhythm.</h1>
+<p class="intro">A little harmony for your type. Explore how modern CSS brings mixed fonts<br class="desktop-break"> into balance, one x-height at a time.</p>
+<div class="toolbar"><div class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Demo view"><button id="playground-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="playground">Playground</button><button id="reference-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="reference" tabindex="-1">CSS reference</button></div><span class="badge">✧ &nbsp; Powered by font-size-adjust</span></div>
+<section id="playground" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="playground-tab">
+<div class="workspace">
+<article class="card"><div class="card-top"><div class="card-title"><span class="number">01</span>Mixed fonts</div><span class="small-label">Automatic harmony</span></div><div class="preview"><div class="preview-label">Sans-serif meets monospace</div><div id="mixed-fonts-container"><p>Good typography is in the details.<br>Even when you mix in <code>inline code</code>,<br>everything should feel like it belongs.</p></div></div><div class="controls"><label class="toggle-label"><input type="checkbox" class="switch" id="normalize" checked>Normalize fonts</label><label class="size-control" for="font-size">Size <input type="range" id="font-size" min="16" max="32" value="24"><output id="size-output" for="font-size">24px</output></label></div></article>
+<article class="card"><div class="card-top"><div class="card-title"><span class="number">02</span>Independent theme</div><span class="small-label">Fixed proportions</span></div><div class="preview theme-preview"><div class="preview-label">A different family. Its own rules.</div><div id="independent-theme-container"><p>A quieter kind of type.<br>Different in character,<br><em>balanced by design.</em></p></div></div><div class="controls"><span>Locked x-height ratio</span><span class="metric">0.50</span></div></article>
+</div>
+<article class="card code-card"><div class="code-header"><span class="file"><span class="file-icon" aria-hidden="true">{ }</span> The CSS behind the balance</span><button class="copy" id="copy-css"><span aria-hidden="true">▢</span> <span id="copy-label" aria-live="polite">Copy CSS</span></button></div><div class="code-grid"><pre><code><span class="comment">/* Match the primary font automatically */</span>
+<span class="selector">#mixed-fonts-container</span> {
+  <span class="property">font-size-adjust</span>: <span class="value">from-font</span>;
+}</code></pre><pre><code><span class="comment">/* Give an independent theme a fixed ratio */</span>
+<span class="selector">#independent-theme-container</span> {
+  <span class="property">font-size-adjust</span>: <span class="value">0.5</span>;
+}</code></pre></div></article>
+<div class="insight"><span class="info-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><p><strong>It's all about x-height.</strong> Fonts at the same size can look surprisingly different. <code>font-size-adjust</code> normalizes their perceived height, keeping your text comfortable and consistent.</p></div>
+</section>
+<section class="card reference" id="reference" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="reference-tab" hidden><h2>One property, two approaches.</h2><p><code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code> takes the x-height ratio from the primary font. Inline code inherits that ratio, so its monospace family stays visually balanced with the surrounding text.</p><p><code>font-size-adjust: 0.5</code> sets an explicit x-height to font-size ratio for the independent theme. At a font size of 24px, this targets a 12px x-height.</p><p>Both containers keep a unitless line height. Older browsers receive fallback sizing through <code>@supports</code>, while supporting browsers adjust the font metrics automatically.</p></section>
+<footer><span>A small exploration of the modern web.</span><span><span class="footer-mark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span> Made for the details.</span></footer>
+</main>
+<script>
+const mixed = document.getElementById('mixed-fonts-container');
+const normalize = document.getElementById('normalize');
+normalize.addEventListener('change', () => { mixed.style.fontSizeAdjust = normalize.checked ? 'from-font' : 'none'; });
+document.getElementById('font-size').addEventListener('input', (event) => {
+  const size = Number(event.target.value);
+  mixed.style.fontSize = `${size / 16}rem`;
+  document.getElementById('size-output').value = `${size}px`;
+});
+const tabs = [...document.querySelectorAll('[role="tab"]')];
+function selectTab(tab) {
+  for (const item of tabs) {
+    const active = item === tab;
+    item.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(active));
+    item.tabIndex = active ? 0 : -1;
+    document.getElementById(item.getAttribute('aria-controls')).hidden = !active;
+  }
+}
+for (const tab of tabs) {
+  tab.addEventListener('click', () => selectTab(tab));
+  tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
+    if (!['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Home', 'End'].includes(event.key)) return;
+    event.preventDefault();
+    const next = event.key === 'Home' ? tabs[0] : event.key === 'End' ? tabs[tabs.length - 1] : tabs[(tabs.indexOf(tab) + (event.key === 'ArrowRight' ? 1 : tabs.length - 1)) % tabs.length];
+    selectTab(next); next.focus();
+  });
+}
+const css = `#mixed-fonts-container {\n  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n  font-size-adjust: from-font;\n}\n\n#mixed-fonts-container code {\n  font-family: "Courier New", monospace;\n  font-size: 1em;\n}\n\n#independent-theme-container {\n  font-family: Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;\n  font-size-adjust: 0.5;\n}\n\n@supports not (font-size-adjust: from-font) {\n  #mixed-fonts-container { line-height: 1.85; }\n  #mixed-fonts-container code { font-size: .92em; }\n}\n\n@supports not (font-size-adjust: 0.5) {\n  #independent-theme-container { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.7; }\n}`;
+document.getElementById('copy-css').addEventListener('click', async () => {
+  const label = document.getElementById('copy-label');
+  try { await navigator.clipboard.writeText(css); label.textContent = 'Copied!'; }
+  catch { label.textContent = 'Select CSS below'; const range = document.createRange(); range.selectNodeContents(document.querySelector('.code-grid')); const selection = window.getSelection(); selection.removeAllRanges(); selection.addRange(range); }
+  setTimeout(() => { label.textContent = 'Copy CSS'; }, 2500);
+});
+</script>
+</body>
