+# Homepage components
+
+Import the desired ES module once, then use its element in any static page.
+Each component owns an open shadow root, a cloned template, and local styles.
+Content stays in semantic light DOM slots, so text and links remain available
+when JavaScript is disabled. Global CSS should style layout and theme tokens;
+component appearance belongs in its module.
+
+```html
+<script type="module" src="./components/coffee-card.js"></script>
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="title">Maple Oat Latte</h3>
+  <p>Creamy oat milk with Vermont maple syrup.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/seasonal"
+     aria-label="View details for Maple Oat Latte">View Details</a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+- `coffee-card`: `title`, default description, and `action` slots. Use the
+  heading level appropriate to the surrounding page. Keep link names specific
+  to the coffee. Exposes `::part(card)` and `--card-background`.
+- `coffee-hero`: `title`, default supporting content, and `action` slots.
+  Exposes `::part(hero)` and `--hero-image` (a CSS image value).
+- `site-navigation`: `brand` and default link slots. Place links directly in
+  the default slot; `data-action="logout"` supplies the outlined treatment.
+  Exposes `::part(navigation)`. Below 48rem, a native button toggles the links;
+  Escape closes them and restores focus. Tab uses normal link order. Resizing
+  updates visibility and avoids leaving focus in hidden links. Listener cleanup
+  supports removing and reconnecting the same instance.
+
