+# Daily Grind components
+
+Load the component modules with `<script type="module">`. They use native custom
+elements and Shadow DOM; no framework, dependencies, or build step is required.
+Content stays in the page as light DOM, so headings and links remain available
+when JavaScript is unavailable. Supply semantic headings and native anchor links.
+
+```html
+<coffee-card>
+  <h3 slot="heading">House Blend</h3>
+  <p>A balanced everyday coffee.</p>
+  <a slot="action" href="/menu/house" aria-label="View details for House Blend">
+    View Details
+  </a>
+</coffee-card>
+```
+
+- `coffee-card`: `heading`, default description, and `action` slots. Use a heading
+  level appropriate to the surrounding page; built-in heading styles target `h3`.
+- `coffee-hero`: `heading` (`h1`), default intro, and `action` slots. Override the
+  decorative background with `--hero-image: url(...)` on the element.
+- `site-navigation`: `brand` (home link) and default navigation link slots.
+  `data-emphasis` adds the outlined treatment to a link. Below 701px, a native
+  button toggles the navigation and exposes its state through `aria-expanded`.
+  Tab follows normal link order; Escape closes the menu and returns focus to its
+  button. Wide layouts expose every link. Event listeners are removed when the
+  element disconnects and restored when it reconnects.
+
+Components inherit typography and support the existing `--primary` and
+`--accent` theme properties. Layout outside the components (such as the card
+grid) belongs to the page. Component styles live inside their shadow roots;
+`styles.js` provides shared focus and action styles. Keep consumer styles for
+slotted content minimal because page styles can also affect that content.
+
+The homepage keeps real routes on every action. Components do not intercept
+navigation or introduce placeholder ordering or account behavior.
