@@ -15,3 +15,35 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Browser agent tools (WebMCP)
+
+The shared layout progressively registers client-side tools when the browser supports
+`document.modelContext` (or the earlier `navigator.modelContext`). Browsers without
+WebMCP keep the same interactive controls. No MCP server is required.
+
+- `get_articles` lists article slugs and summaries.
+- `open_search` opens the search flyout, exposing its `search_articles` form tool.
+  The required `query` field searches titles and summaries and returns matches.
+- `open_reading_list` opens the reading-list flyout, exposing
+  `manage_reading_list`. Its `action` is `view`, `add`, or `remove`; `slug` is
+  required for changes. Results include saved slugs and article details. Repeated
+  add/remove actions are idempotent. Changes use the current browser session.
+- `brew_coffee`, `get_plant_stats`, `get_tide_levels`, and
+  `get_article_popularity` expose the article API utilities. Popularity requires
+  an `id` (article slug). Utility results include `ok`, `status`, `redirected`,
+  `url`, and `data`, preserving intentional HTTP errors and redirects in the
+  debugging demos. Fetch/network failures reject the tool invocation.
+
+Form tools read actual submitted fields, update the visible UI, and return results
+through `SubmitEvent.respondWith` for agent submissions. They also work through
+normal submit buttons. Flyout tools exist while their forms are open; use the
+corresponding `open_*` tool to make them available. Imperative tools are removed
+and registered again across Astro client-side navigation without clearing tools
+owned by other scripts.
+
+API references: [imperative WebMCP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/imperative-api)
+and [declarative forms](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/ai/webmcp/declarative-api).
+
+Run `pnpm test` for mocked client-side tool tests and `pnpm run build` for the
+production build. These checks do not launch a browser or a server.
